      "id": 65947,
      "name": "Katsue",
      "username": "Katsue",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/katsue/{size}/2012_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-06-15T23:52:25.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Reckless\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/48/2467_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Reckless:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Devastation of Indines features Legacy as a fighter kit with four Strikers (cards representing fighters in the game that can \"assist\" the main fighter) as the remaining Freedom Five members (which can be used with Legacy or with other fighters).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Legacy's kind of a weird one as far as crossovers go because promo characters for Devastation aren't legal in official tournament play. So even though in principle there's no storyline reason in either universe that Legacy couldn't show up in Indines (via spaceship or interdimensional portal or what have you), it would seem that any such appearance is non-canonical.</p>",
